        "PMC5995863::rubric_card::000::6a984a21e0"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed initial material can be an as-cast or homogenized high-entropy alloy.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11087546::rubric_card::000::3e3b5fbe93",
        "PMC11206460::rubric_card::000::bd033a5c9c",
        "PMC5995863::rubric_card::000::6a984a21e0"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "High-pressure and high-temperature treatment can modify a high-entropy-alloy microstructure and improve both strength and ductility.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11087546::rubric_card::000::3e3b5fbe93"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Alloying additions can change phase constitution and mechanical properties in refractory high-entropy alloys.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10759803::rubric_card::000::1894dec07a"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Room-temperature or elevated-temperature uniaxial tensile or compression testing can be used to assess the proposed behavior.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11087546::rubric_card::000::3e3b5fbe93",
        "PMC11206460::rubric_card::000::bd033a5c9c",
        "PMC5995863::rubric_card::000::6a984a21e0"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Phase composition, microstructure, and defects mediate the ductile–brittle–ductile transition.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11087546::rubric_card::000::3e3b5fbe93",
        "PMC5995863::rubric_card::000::6a984a21e0"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Changing a continuous ordered B2 matrix into a weakly ordered BCC structure can transform a brittle refractory high-entropy alloy into a much more ductile state.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5995863::rubric_card::000::6a984a21e0"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "A continuous reticulated structure of a hard Laves phase can hinder crack propagation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A continuous reticulated Laves-phase structure can enhance ductility.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Activation of dislocations, stacking faults, microbands, and deformation twins produces strain delocalization.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Activation of multiple deformation mechanisms enhances work hardening.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed interventions can improve both ductility and strength in high-entropy alloys.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11087546::rubric_card::000::3e3b5fbe93"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed interventions may produce a ductile–brittle–ductile transition.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Conventional alloys generally have limited ductility and strength relative to the proposed high-entropy-alloy design.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The ductile–brittle–ductile transition is sensitive to phase composition, microstructure, and defects.",
